From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:23:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] generalise the legacy sync scheduler shim to execution
 provenance

Replaces the SHA-256-keyed per-plugin rule table with one question asked of the
platform: on whose behalf is this thread running. LophinyaExecutionProvenance is
the single model of that answer - region, global region, or one entity - with
capture, inheritance, lifetime and clearing defined in one place instead of
spread across the dispatchers.

The rule table could only ever work for the exact jar it was written against. The
production server proved it: the table held EssentialsX 2.22.1-dev+12-776f709, the
server runs dev+17-382de4f, so every rule missed and User.updateActivityOnChat
went back to throwing UnsupportedOperationException out of AsyncPlayerChatEvent -
which aborts EssentialsX's chat handler entirely. Keying compatibility on a file
hash means an unmodified plugin loses support the moment it is updated. It is
deleted rather than extended.

What replaces it for that case is not a rule but a missing owner type. Paper
dispatches AsyncPlayerChatEvent on "Async Chat Thread - #N", a pooled thread that
owns nothing, so a legacy scheduleSyncDelayedTask from a listener had nowhere to
go. But the platform knows whose work it is: a PlayerEvent names exactly one
player, and Folia's EntityScheduler is the documented API for scheduling that
player's work "from any thread context", surviving the player moving between
regions and worlds and reporting failure rather than running once the player is
gone. PaperEventManager establishes that owner for the duration of the dispatch
and removes it in a finally, so a pooled chat thread cannot carry one player's
owner into the next player's message.

Nothing is inferred from the plugin's runnable, and everything that was rejected
for lack of an owner still is: a bare async thread, an async event with no single
player (AsyncPlayerConnectionConfigureEvent has no Player at all), and a second
async hop, since inheritance is deliberately bounded at one. A redispatched task
that reaches into another region still fails at the access, not at the schedule.

Also fixes cancellation, which the redispatch path had quietly broken:
CraftScheduler.cancelTask(int) looks the id up in maps a redispatched task was
never in, so BukkitTask.cancel() was a no-op and a repeating task ran until its
plugin was disabled. LophinyaDispatchedTasks supplies the missing lookup, and the
task body re-checks the cancelled flag that CraftScheduler's own queue used to
check for it.

Successful redispatch is a working compatibility path, so it now logs INFO once
per distinct callsite and DEBUG thereafter, instead of WARN on every single
dispatch - which is what was flooding the production console.

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperEventManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperEventManager.java
index 0fce6dc8bffc341da2e7242422b4153b2743aa44..8316921c05f4bc791f5249df0e72dbb09f0cf5c4 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperEventManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperEventManager.java
@@ -62,6 +62,29 @@ class PaperEventManager {
         }
         // Leaves end - skip bot
 
+        // Lecithin start - execution provenance for an async event that names one player
+        // An asynchronous event is dispatched on a thread that owns nothing, so a legacy
+        // scheduleSyncDelayedTask from inside one of these listeners has nowhere to go and is
+        // rejected - taking the rest of the listener down with it (measured: EssentialsX's
+        // cancel-afk-on-chat aborted chat formatting and delivery entirely). But the platform is not
+        // in the dark about whose work it is: a PlayerEvent names exactly one player, and Folia's
+        // EntityScheduler is the documented API for scheduling that player's work from any thread.
+        // Establishing that owner for the duration of the dispatch is what lets the legacy call
+        // reach it. Nothing is inferred from the plugin's runnable, the scope is removed in a
+        // finally so a pooled chat thread never carries one player's owner into the next player's
+        // message, and every event with no single player owner still fails closed.
+        final fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinExecutionProvenance.Owner lecithin$owner =
+            fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinExecutionProvenance.ownerOfAsyncEvent(event);
+        if (lecithin$owner != null) {
+            final RegisteredListener[] lecithin$listeners = listeners;
+            fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinExecutionProvenance.runWithScope(lecithin$owner, () -> this.dispatch(lecithin$listeners, event));
+            return;
+        }
+        this.dispatch(listeners, event);
+    }
+
+    private void dispatch(RegisteredListener[] listeners, @NotNull Event event) {
+        // Lecithin end - execution provenance for an async event that names one player
         for (RegisteredListener registration : listeners) {
             if (!registration.getPlugin().isEnabled()) {
                 continue;
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
index f7552dcbaa1c9060254bd6490324a022c8d25937..2c5792223d2f78ce0bfa991182f2be378ca9e90c 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
@@ -278,6 +278,15 @@ class PaperPluginInstanceManager {
         }
         // Lecithin end - restored async scheduler: cancel Bukkit tasks on disable, like Paper does
 
+        // Lecithin start - cancel any legacy sync tasks this plugin had redispatched onto Folia
+        // schedulers. Same reasoning as the block above: those tasks are in none of Bukkit's queues,
+        // so without this a disabled plugin's redispatched repeating task would keep running forever.
+        try {
+            fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinDispatchedTasks.cancelAll(plugin);
+        } catch (Throwable ignored) {
+        }
+        // Lecithin end - cancel redispatched legacy sync tasks
+
         // Paper start - Folia schedulers
         try {
             this.server.getGlobalRegionScheduler().cancelTasks(plugin);
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java
index a5931d31a04bf59bec516d8b29f0082483e9ee8e..9cfed92eaee7811271708c0615c5f092caa9d866 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java
@@ -11,11 +11,12 @@ class CraftAsyncTask extends CraftTask {
 
     private final LinkedList<BukkitWorker> workers = new LinkedList<BukkitWorker>();
     private final Map<Integer, CraftTask> runners;
-    // Lecithin start - carry the scheduling thread's context into this async task
-    // Captured here, not in run(): the constructor still runs on the thread that asked for the task,
-    // which is the only moment the context is a fact rather than a guess.
-    private final fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinCallerContextDispatch.CapturedContext lecithin$schedulingContext =
-        fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinCallerContextDispatch.captureCallerContext();
+    // Lecithin start - carry the scheduling thread's execution provenance into this async task
+    // Captured here, not in run(): the field initialiser still runs on the thread that asked for the
+    // task, which is the only moment the owner is a fact rather than a guess. See
+    // LecithinExecutionProvenance for why this crosses exactly one async hop and no further.
+    private final fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinExecutionProvenance.Owner lecithin$schedulingOwner =
+        fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinExecutionProvenance.captureForAsyncHandoff();
     // Lecithin end
 
     CraftAsyncTask(final Map<Integer, CraftTask> runners, final Plugin plugin, final Object task, final int id, final long delay) {
@@ -60,8 +61,8 @@ class CraftAsyncTask extends CraftTask {
         }
         Throwable thrown = null;
         try {
-            // Lecithin start - make the scheduling thread's context visible for this body only
-            fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinCallerContextDispatch.runInherited(this.lecithin$schedulingContext, super::run);
+            // Lecithin start - make the scheduling thread's owner visible for this body only
+            fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinExecutionProvenance.runWithScope(this.lecithin$schedulingOwner, super::run);
             // Lecithin end
         } catch (final Throwable t) {
             thrown = t;
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
index f1518ce64edaa2d40f9c9038bb489fa2439ed826..954ab2b7e6812d5043bfccc801306bbcbf31688d 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
@@ -273,6 +273,16 @@ public class CraftScheduler implements BukkitScheduler {
         if (task != null) {
             task.cancel0();
         }
+        // Lecithin start - a redispatched task is cancellable through the API the plugin used
+        // A legacy sync task that LecithinCallerContextDispatch redispatched onto a Folia scheduler
+        // is in none of the maps above, so this cancel used to be a silent no-op and a repeating task
+        // ran until its plugin was disabled. The registry supplies the missing lookup; cancel0() has
+        // to happen here because it is package-private to this package.
+        final CraftTask redispatched = fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinDispatchedTasks.cancelById(taskId);
+        if (redispatched != null) {
+            redispatched.cancel0();
+        }
+        // Lecithin end - a redispatched task is cancellable through the API the plugin used
         // Lecithin start - restored async scheduler: cancellation must not die on sync-side bookkeeping
         // The guard task below goes through handle(), which regionised threading rejects - the caller
         // would get an UnsupportedOperationException *after* the async-side cancel already succeeded.
@@ -334,6 +344,10 @@ public class CraftScheduler implements BukkitScheduler {
                     runner.cancel0();
                 }
             }
+            // Lecithin - redispatched tasks are in no runners map; see cancelTask(int)
+            for (final CraftTask redispatched : fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinDispatchedTasks.cancelAll(plugin)) {
+                redispatched.cancel0();
+            }
             return;
         }
         // Lecithin end - restored async scheduler: same reasoning as cancelTask(int)
@@ -550,16 +564,20 @@ public class CraftScheduler implements BukkitScheduler {
             this.addTask(task);
             return task;
         }
-        // Lecithin start - redispatch a rejected sync task to the caller's own execution context
-        // (see LecithinCallerContextDispatch). Only reached for sync tasks on the main (non-async)
-        // scheduler - exactly the case stock Folia has no home for.
+        // Lecithin start - general legacy sync scheduler dispatch
+        // Only reached for sync tasks on the main (non-async) scheduler - exactly the case stock
+        // Folia has no home for. There is no plugin list, no jar hash and no class name involved:
+        // LecithinCallerContextDispatch asks LecithinExecutionProvenance whose work this thread is
+        // doing and dispatches to the Folia scheduler that owns the answer. It returns null, and so
+        // still falls through to the throw below, whenever nothing is known - which is the fail-closed
+        // case and stays that way.
         if (!this.isAsyncScheduler && task.isSync()) {
             final CraftTask redispatched = fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinCallerContextDispatch.tryDispatch(task, delay, task.getPeriod());
             if (redispatched != null) {
                 return redispatched;
             }
         }
-        // Lecithin end - redispatch to the caller's own execution context
+        // Lecithin end - general legacy sync scheduler dispatch
         throw new UnsupportedOperationException(fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinSchedulerDiagnostics.reportRejected(
             task.getOwner(), delay, task.getPeriod(), !task.isSync()));
         // Lecithin end - restore Bukkit async scheduler semantics + diagnostic guard
